  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of Member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In its report published in 2022, the CEACR expressed satisfaction with Georgia&#x2019;s progress in relation to Conventions 87 and 98. Between May 2019, when the reform process was initiated, and September 2020 when the reform package was adopted, the ILO provided extensive support in the development of the package of the Labour Code and a new Law on labour Inspection, by providing comparative legislative information, drafting amendments,  organising consultations with the Government, social partners and other stakeholders, and participating in Parliamentary Hearings. The main goal of the reform was to improve conformity of Georgia&#x2019;s labour laws with relevant ILO Conventions and the EU Directives under the EU-Georgia Association Agreement to which Georgia committed to harmonise its legislation.</narrative>
   </description>
